From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:38:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/43] Shaders: fix MIMG 3D Z texel offsets, a16 offset
 truncation, and cubemap sample_d LOD

Fix three MIMG texture-sampling bugs in `Lower::image`:

1. **a16 offset truncation**: `offset_word` read `addr_val(self, 0)` instead
   of `addr_u32(self, 0)`. Because `addr_val` masks to 16 bits when `a16`
   is set, bits `[21:16]` (the 3D Z offset) were zeroed on `a16` samples.
2. **Dropped 3D Z texel offset & non-sample-60 constant folding**: Offset
   extraction capped at `.min(2)`, silently dropping the Z offset (`bits
   [21:16]`) on 3D textures (`offsets == 3`). Furthermore, folding constant
   offset words in `-8..=7` to DXIL immediate constants only ran inside the
   pixel `op == 60` arm, leaving `image_sample_lz_o` (`op == 62`) and
   compute `image_sample_o` with non-immediate offsets rejected by `dxil.dll`.
   Move constant-offset folding into the shared `offset_word` block and
   extract all `offsets` axes (X, Y, Z).
3. **Cubemap `image_sample_d` LOD inflated by `LOG2_E` (`1.4427x`)**: DXIL
   unary opcode `23` (`dx.op.unary.f32(23, x)`, `Log`) is already base-2
   logarithm (`log2`), not natural log (`ln`). Multiplying its result by
   `LOG2_E` pushed every cubemap gradient sample ~1.44x higher in the mip
   chain.

Add `mimg_3d_sample_offset_preserves_z_and_a16` and
`mimg_cube_sample_d_selects_exact_log2_mip` (with `#[cfg(test)]`
`View::Texture3D` and `View::CubeMips` support in `emit::host`) verified
on hardware D3D12, WARP, and `dxil.dll`.

(cherry picked from commit 61e28e68341492384c95da6596c3e7fc7cce8222)
(cherry picked from commit c4335bb5bedc77e9ca7d15844dbcd0946f203490)
